MODEL WEIGHTS
=============

The weights of the proposed model (the two "Proposed (joint, …)" checkpoints listed in
weights/CHECKSUMS.tsv) are derived from Stable Diffusion v1-5 by fine-tuning, including its
autoencoder:
   https://huggingface.co/stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-v1-5
   Copyright (c) 2022 Robin Rombach and Patrick Esser and contributors
   CreativeML Open RAIL-M License (LICENSES/CreativeML-OpenRAIL-M.txt)
These weights are distributed under that licence, including the use-based restrictions in its
Attachment A, which apply to anyone who uses or redistributes them and must be passed on with them.
They have been modified from the original by fine-tuning on sky images.

All other weights in weights/ were trained from scratch for this work and are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, like the code.


DATA
====

No SIRTA data is distributed with this repository. The sky images and irradiance measurements used
by the paper and by preprocessing/ are provided by the SIRTA atmospheric observatory under its own
data policy and must be obtained from SIRTA. Work that uses them should acknowledge SIRTA ("The authors
would like to acknowledge SIRTA for providing the data used in this study.") and cite:
   Haeffelin, M., et al. (2005). SIRTA, a ground-based atmospheric observatory for cloud and aerosol
   research. Annales Geophysicae, 23(2), 253-275. https://doi.org/10.5194/angeo-23-253-2005

The stored forecasts in prediction_samples/ are model outputs and contain no SIRTA measurements.


SYNTHETIC IMAGES
================

samples/synthetic_2023/ contains no SIRTA observations: its sky images are generated by a diffusion model
whose image decoder is the Stable Diffusion v1.4 VAE
   https://huggingface.co/CompVis/stable-diffusion-v1-4
   CreativeML Open RAIL-M License (LICENSES/CreativeML-OpenRAIL-M.txt)
and that model was trained on real SIRTA 2023 sky images. As with any use of SIRTA's data, please
acknowledge SIRTA and cite Haeffelin, M., et al. (2005), above.
